    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "For many middle school students in China, the Zhongkao, or high school entrance exam, is a major source of stress. To enter a good high school, students often spend hours studying every night. But now, new reforms are on the way to make school life a little "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In several cities and provinces, biology and geography will no longer "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " toward the total Zhongkao score. This new policy will "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "take effect",
            "ref": "v-effect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " next summer. Cities like Beijing have already cut the number of scored subjects. Education officials say this "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " will help break the “rat race” in school and ease the heavy burden on students."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "This news has sparked a huge "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". On Weibo, the topic has been viewed more than 50 million times. Many parents "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the reform. They hope their children will have more time for sports, hobbies, and sleep. “It gives children more "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "energy",
            "ref": "v-energy"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for their overall development,” one parent wrote."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, some people are worried. They think biology and geography are important for "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the world around us. If these subjects are not on the exam, will students still study them "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Other parents worry that the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "pressure",
            "ref": "v-pressure"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " will not really "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "disappear",
            "ref": "v-disappear"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They fear that the competition will just move to the Gaokao, China’s even more "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " university entrance exam."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Experts believe the Zhongkao should be less about high-pressure ranking and more about helping students "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". As China admits more students into high schools, the goal is to focus on real learning instead of intensive "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". For now, many students hope these changes will bring them a more balanced and happy future."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
